.TH garuda-toolbox-boot-set 1  "garuda-toolbox 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-boot\-set \- Change one setting of the boot menu, then regenerate it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox boot set\fR [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change one setting of the boot menu, then regenerate it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Do not ask, carry the change out. Needed without a terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the plan and stop, without asking and without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON Lines instead of text, for scripts. Needs `\-\-yes` or `\-\-dry\-run`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
What to change
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
default: The entry that boots by default, as `boot entries` prints it
.IP \(bu 2
timeout: Seconds the menu shows, 0 to 300
.IP \(bu 2
remember: Boot the entry that booted last (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
submenus: Group older kernels in a submenu (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
os\-prober: List other systems in the menu (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
quiet: Hide the kernel\*(Aqs messages while booting (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
splash: Show a splash screen while booting (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
mitigations\-off: Turn the CPU mitigations off (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
sysrq: Allow the magic `SysRq` keys (on or off)
.IP \(bu 2
background: The picture behind the menu: a full path, or `none`
.IP \(bu 2
theme: The menu\*(Aqs theme: the full path of a theme.txt, or `none`
.IP \(bu 2
plymouth: The Plymouth theme shown while booting
.RE
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
The new value: an entry id, seconds, on or off, a full path or `none`, or a Plymouth theme
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox boot set timeout 3
  garuda\-toolbox boot set quiet off
  garuda\-toolbox boot set plymouth bgrt
  garuda\-toolbox boot set background none
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-boot(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
